      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, honestly, I’m just... I’m so exhausted. I’m here because it’s been a full year of this, and it is completely wearing me down. \n\nYou see, I’m a phlebotomist, so I draw blood all day. I know how the system works, I know how the tubes are routed to the lab, and I know exactly how the charts are updated in the electronic medical records. And for the past twelve months, I have been trying—literally trying everything I can think of, making phone calls, tracking timestamps—to prove that someone inside the clinic system is intentionally changing or holding back parts of my dad’s lab results. \n\nI was looking right at the screen when his initial metabolic panels came back, and I saw the raw values. I know what they were. But then later, the official chart was completely different. Certain markers were just gone or altered to look normal. And no matter how many doctors I talk to about it, or how many times my own family members tell me to just let it go and that his numbers are fine, I *know* what I saw. The finalized chart does not match the initial data, and nobody will investigate it. They keep telling me I'm just stressed or that I misread the screen, but I do this for a living! I know someone is manipulating his file, and trying to get anyone to just look at the discrepancies and listen to me is... it's just draining the life out of me. I can't just pretend it's fine when I know they're hiding something about his health.",
