      "doctor_question": "Have you ever heard voices, sounds, or whispering that other people couldn't hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Voices? No. No, absolutely not. I mean... I know exactly why you're asking that, because when you tell people that official medical records are being actively altered, they immediately jump to, 'Oh, she must be hearing things, she must be losing her grip.' But I don't hear whispering or voices or... or anything like that. \n\nThe only things I hear are the actual, real sounds happening in the clinic, you know, the hum of the centrifuges spinning down the gold-top tubes, or the overhead paging system, or the phones ringing off the hook at the front desk. I am completely, one-hundred-percent grounded in reality, which is exactly why this whole situation with my dad's chart is so incredibly frustrating to me. I'm not talking about some... some phantom voice whispering in my ear; I am talking about raw, numerical data that I saw with my own two eyes on a high-definition monitor at workstation number four. \n\nI don't need to hear voices when I have actual visual proof of what the metabolic panel originally said before it was scrubbed. Well, proof that they keep erasing and denying, anyway. But no, to actually answer your question, I don't hear sounds that aren't there. I'm not hallucinating. I just see what *is* there, and I see what they are trying so hard to hide from me, and nobody will just sit down and look at the screen with me to see it for themselves.",
