      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Physical health? No, I don't have any medical conditions like that. I mean, honestly, I'm perfectly healthy. I don't have high blood pressure, no diabetes, no thyroid issues... I don't even get seasonal allergies, really. I take a multivitamin in the morning, sometimes a little vitamin D in the winter when it gets dark so early, but that's it. I don't take any prescription medications. \n\nI actually had a full physical myself just a few months ago, right before the clinic switched over to the new insurance provider for the staff, because I wanted to make sure everything was documented under the old system just in case... well, you know, just to have a clean baseline. And my labs were completely pristine. My fasting glucose was perfect, my lipid panel was well within normal limits, my CBC was completely unremarkable. \n\nSo, physically, I am fine. Which is honestly a blessing, because if I were dealing with some kind of chronic illness on top of the sheer exhaustion of trying to get someone to pay attention to what's happening with my dad's chart, I don't know how I would manage. It takes so much energy just tracking the digital footprints of his records and calling the lab supervisors and trying to get a straight answer out of the IT department. If I had, you know, chronic pain or something, I wouldn't have the stamina to keep pushing for the truth. But no, my body is holding up just fine. It's just my patience that's completely worn out. I am physically as healthy as a horse, I promise you.",
